    {
      "title": "Kikujiro movie review & film summary - Roger Ebert",
      "snippet": "\"Kikujiro\" is the last sort of film you would expect him to make-even though he skews the material toward his hard-boiled style and away from the obvious opportunities for sentiment. Kikujiro, known only as \"Mister\" to the little boy, is played by Kitano as a man who is willing to seem a clown, but keeps his thoughts to himself.",
